

📘 CORE USER MANUAL — DEVELOPER COMMAND GUIDE

Authoring Laws, Packaging Blueprints, Deploying Worlds, and Operating the Network Node

1. Overview

This manual teaches developers how to:

create and version Laws

assemble Geometry Blueprints

define World Scenarios

sign and encrypt artifacts using your identity

submit workloads to the network node

verify responses and ledger entries

It assumes:

access to the repository

access to the public key

access to the local CLI or remote socket interface

2. Authoring New Laws (Kernel)

A Law defines the mathematical rules governing a world.

2.1 File Structure

Each Law is a JSON object:

{
  "law_id": "string",
  "version": "number",
  "parent_version": "number|null",
  "equations": {},
  "constraints": {},
  "metadata": {}
}

2.2 Versioning Rules

Increment version for any change

Set parent_version to previous version

Ledger automatically records lineage

2.3 Validation

Run:

Kernel Validator

Equation Consistency Check

3. Packaging Geometry Blueprints (DAGs)

Blueprints define the structural layout of components and transforms.

3.1 Node Definition

Each node must specify:

kernel binding

input/output types

deterministic behavior

3.2 DAG Rules

No cycles

No unconnected nodes

No unused outputs

3.3 Pre‑Execution Tests

Run:

DAG Integrity Check

Kernel Binding Test

